WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.160
You are challenged to match the awesome skills of your opponents to gain the title in the World Super Championships of Tag Team Wrestling!

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:30.320
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.220
I'm Mike. I'm Joe.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:33.780
I'm Sean. And I'm Sam.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.920
Guys, tag team wrestling.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.580
Woo! Yay.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:42.440
Yeah, I felt that from the room, but more importantly, Sean hasn't even reacted yet.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.660
More importantly, though, we're talking about a Data East game.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:52.620
Oh, man. Yeah, a company that doesn't really have an amazing reputation and is now bankrupt.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.440
Yeah. Woo!

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.200
Hey, they got the first third party game in there, didn't they?

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:04.600
Yeah, this is the, and it seems like we barely talk about that, but every game so far was like Nintendo at least published.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:08.620
Mm-hmm. Uh, developed was sometimes handled by intelligence systems.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.660
Or, um, who did Ten Yard Fight?

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.560
Iram. Did that.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.540
So they did Tenured Fight and also Kung Fu.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:19.520
Yes. So, you know, there were other parties in there for sure,

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:22.120
but this is the first game that Nintendo has allowed

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:23.960
without their publishing seal on it.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.780
Now, of course, it still has the Nintendo seal.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.400
It has the seal of approval.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:32.800
I guess we'll be the guests of if that matters anymore.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.420
We're just the true approvers.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.380
Yeah, we'll judge if it still deserves that quality seal.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.800
But let's go right into first impressions.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.000
Joe, what do you got for me?

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:43.260
I think the first thing I thought was like,

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.200
what is going on in this game?

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.300
Because it seemed like.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:49.640
This is real fast.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:51.580
You're in the ring with an opponent.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:54.940
It's pretty simple wrestling, but it seemed pretty random

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:56.840
whether I'm hitting him, he's hitting me.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.280
I mean, I'm doing the same thing every time.

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:00.040
Sometimes I get a hit. Sometimes he gets a hit.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:03.680
Not a lot of like animation doesn't feel like we're like moving.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:06.020
It was just it was a little confusing at the beginning.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.360
Yeah, I didn't get much better.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:11.260
Sean. Okay, so you you the way you explain it, Joe,

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:16.740
was that you would sometimes get a hit just as often as he would get a hit or the computer would get a hit.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.900
Okay, I'm sure the computer got a hit more often.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.120
I think I know where you're going with this.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.960
Yeah, it was very difficult to get a hit.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.560
This game is is not very user friendly.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:33.660
The computer seems to have no problem just doing like a frame perfect interrupt of whatever you are about to do.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:41.380
It was it was wrestling, but it was as if you were a tiny, tiny boy and you were wrestling the big man.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:48.520
Yeah. Yeah, I felt like I was doing like I read the manual.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:56.880
Well, first of all, I read the manual before going into this and I felt like I missed something because I just got my ass kicked like immediately.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.000
There are only seven pages to that manual, aren't there?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:05.480
Yeah, and I I didn't I didn't know what was happening and I kept trying and I just I felt like it was cheap.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:12.440
I felt like I just I was wondering at one point like did they actually like allow you to fight in this game?

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:13.960
Like I know it was by a different developer.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:17.280
Maybe it's like how long can you last in the ring with this guy?

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:18.440
It's a kind of wrestling.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:27.440
Yeah. So, yeah, my first impression was just that that is such a weird way to handle grappling in this game.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:35.220
Oh, yeah. For the uninformed, what you do is you'll punch with a and it will let out the tiniest punch animation.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:38.760
It looks like it's barely like the guy's barely reaching across to his opponent.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:49.720
But if you're lucky enough, you will register that as a hit and then a like screen will come on with the attack that you yeah, a menu with like what attack you might do.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:53.200
And then you can toggle through B in three seconds time.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:54.360
You have to hit it over and over.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:58.100
As many times you can just hit B like I think you get like four or five different moves.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:03:59.420
There's a ton of different moves.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.740
Really? Yeah. How many?

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:04.220
I don't remember exactly, but I remember seeing a lot of different.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:05.620
There's like six, seven, eight.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:07.240
OK, that's way more than four.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.760
Four. That's at least two more than four.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:09.740
He's got me there.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:14.840
Anyway, so you cycle through them and then that's the move you wind up and then that's the move you wind up doing.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:17.460
Well, you got to press A on the move.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.800
Otherwise, your guy just does nothing.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.060
But that's what screws you over.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:26.660
I understand cycling with B because I guess you, you know, even though you're on a menu screen, you should be able to cycle with the D-pad.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.080
But let's say you couldn't, right?

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.140
And you need to use B.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:39.500
To reconfirm with A, the problem there is that you're mashing the buttons so much that you just wind up, at least me, I always wind up doing the very first attack.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.840
Well, yeah. But Mike, that means you're playing the game wrong.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:50.020
You're supposed to know exactly when you're going to hit them and then have the presence of mind to go into menu mode and then do your move.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:51.500
I get the menu mode, I think.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:58.300
I think that it was, because it's like, I think this is one where you look up what the move is in the manual, you know?

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.220
I think it's a manual game.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:05.320
What I mean, though, is that you should never be mashing buttons.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:08.160
But you can only play this game by mashing buttons.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.880
Well, I get that too. And I think that's okay for games, you know, to be a button masher.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:17.960
Because your better moves are near the end with, like, you have to press B like eight times or whatever to get the cool moves.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:25.420
Yeah, but I'm constantly getting, I can't do those cool moves because I'm constantly hitting A and then immediately reconfirming my A, even though I'm just not noticing.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:33.140
My issue with it was I kept pressing B to try and get to the last of it, and then I would never hit A, and so the guy would just hit me again.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:34.680
Can I ask you guys something?

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:38.620
Yes. How frequently did you guys get this menu to come up when you hit that?

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:42.100
Very infrequently. When I connected, I got it.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:44.200
No, I know, but I connected very infrequently.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:47.300
Did you ever connect and not have the menu come up and you just start pinning the guy?

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.260
I've had that only when they're on the floor.

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:51.000
Okay, can I tell you guys something?

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:52.240
Yeah, I'm ready.

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:54.100
I never got the menu to come up.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:56.460
No. Right now, I'm going to go over here panicking.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:57.440
I'm like, what are they talking about?

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:58.780
I'm like, do I just go along with it?

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:00.480
I never got the menu to come up.

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:02.780
A full-blown menu with, like, a border.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:07.660
Yeah, it just tells you one word, and then when you press B again, it cycles to a different word.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:10.320
It'll be like, how did your guys get on the floor?

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:12.020
But I have pinned someone.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.700
Oh, wait, I know exactly what happened.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:15.040
I figured out Joe's situation.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:27.060
So what must have happened is the guy picked you up, and then your tag team partner came in, punched them, knocked them down, and then you went to pin them.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:28.340
Because they were knocked down.

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:29.460
I did get picked up a lot.

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:31.420
It was always the same move that he would use on me.

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:35.300
I thought, I could be wrong, but I thought that I used it on him before, too.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:39.540
But if I didn't have that word come up, maybe it came up, but I didn't even see it, and I was just pressing so fast.

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.780
No, the strong pads always have the upper hand with you.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:48.480
Yeah. I saw it in the manual, because I did eventually go back and read the manual.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:53.280
It's like, what am I missing? I saw in the manual it hit B this many times, and I just never saw that come up.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:54.300
This is fascinating.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:57.180
Yeah. You're bringing a whole different perspective to the game.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.760
I think we should probably get a little more focused, though, first.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:04.840
So I don't want to say let's talk about the objective, because it's wrestling.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:10.020
But the ways to win is either by count out, outside of the ring, a count to 20.

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:13.260
And if both are out, then I honestly don't know what happened.

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:14.880
I'm probably just going to say you lost.

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.320
Yeah, probably. In games like these.

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:20.420
But then the other way is to pin, and is there like a TKO option?

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:22.280
If there is, I never got it.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:23.360
I don't believe so.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:28.000
I think once you get into a pin, you just can't get out when you have zero energy.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.200
You have to mash. It says that in the manual.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:35.360
Yes. It says to mash, but if there's enough of an energy disparity, you're not going to get out.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:36.520
Oh, yes. I hear what you're saying.

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:38.680
I lost every time by pinning.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:46.660
Even in those later WWF games that were popular on the N64, like WrestleMania 2000 and No Mercy,

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:51.540
there comes a point where you've just been beaten down so hard that even when you're getting pinned

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:53.760
and you're trying to break out, it's just not going to happen.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.620
So that's a cool little touch.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:58.360
But this game is missing a lot.

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:06.480
And I think that more so than the menu thing is an interesting way to get around not being able to program

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:07.440
a bunch of different moves.

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:13.900
But I think coming up very soon, we'll see a better way to handle doing different moves in a wrestling game.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:15.060
Better, yeah. Yeah.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:18.740
I'm not saying efficient still, but definitely better.

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:25.760
One thing that I couldn't get over is that there's a point where your opponents just become invincible.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.800
Yeah, they turn red and they just come at you.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.120
That's in the manual, too.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:31.920
It mentions that they start glowing with the angrier they get.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:33.780
If you try to run away or something.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:35.000
But I never glow.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.460
I never become invincible.

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:39.140
That seems really cheap that it doesn't happen for me.

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:46.180
Yeah. I would just like to go back for one moment, Mike, and say that you said that this game has a lot missing.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:47.440
Yes. It's missing a lot.

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:48.740
I would say that's true.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:55.600
But even what is there is just so poorly implemented that there's no way to have fun with this game.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:09:04.280
Like, the only way to do anything is almost locked out just because of how frame perfect you have to be with it.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:14.840
So even if it had more features, if it kept the way that it actually implemented the features it does have, this game would be no better.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.160
I'll say it right now.

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:17.460
The animation is jank.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:21.600
Okay? Yes. The special moves are not very special.

00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:22.860
They don't really feel that cool.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:26.460
Yeah. The tag is almost, like, irrelevant.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:27.600
I feel like I never used the tag.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:28.500
There's no real reason.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.140
I mean, maybe a stamina thing.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:32.440
Like, oh, my guy's really low on health right now, so I'll tag him.

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:33.720
My other guy. Who cares?

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:36.720
Like, the sooner you get out of the match, the better it is for your soul.

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:38.460
The sooner you just shut off the system.

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:40.220
Yeah, exactly. So just end the match.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:43.800
But did anybody actually, like, win a match?

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:45.600
No. I won a match.

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:48.140
I pinned a guy, but didn't hold him down.

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:49.900
You actually won. I actually won a match.

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:51.700
Did your guys do the little dance at the end?

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:53.340
They did. Okay, that makes me feel good.

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:58.160
They did a little dance, and then you immediately fight the same people again, and you're still

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.300
the same people as well.

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:02.240
But they're harder, right? Well, I wouldn't say.

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:06.220
I didn't notice that they were harder, but, you know, like, winning the first one was kind

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:10.640
of a fluke to begin with, so I didn't continue on, really, to continue fighting.

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:15.920
But I played a couple of different fights, and the one that I won, the main strategy was

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:20.580
just every time I was able to get an attack to knock them down, was just to pin them right

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:23.280
away and get closer to that three count each time.

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:28.840
So I don't know. Changing up the number of times you pin, like, if you pin more frequently, that eventually

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:30.280
the ref will just hand it to you.

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:31.820
He'll just do, like, a faster three count.

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:35.840
You notice that when the ref is counting you out or counting your opponent out, that he

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:37.580
has, like, the biggest smile on his face?

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:40.260
Like, he is the happiest to be reffing.

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:41.240
He just likes what he does.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:42.600
It's the most exciting part of his job.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:43.500
He just likes pinning.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:44.740
He's almost out of the game.

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:45.800
He's like, this is it.

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:47.240
I can finally go home.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:50.040
But yeah, it's like an open-mouthed smile.

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:51.740
I mean, it's a very happy smile.

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.660
The other way I won, because I won another match.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:56.780
You won twice? Not in the same sequence.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:58.200
Wow. Was a count-out.

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:00.560
Oh, really? A very cheap count-out.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:03.820
And I found this to probably be the most efficient method for those who want to...

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:05.400
Just keep jumping out and into the ring.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:09.520
What I would do is I would be out there, and then, no, I would actually just continue to

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:15.580
fight him, do different moves and stuff like that, get to, like, a 19 count, jump back in

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:19.140
the ring real fast before he could, and then it counts him out, because...

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:20.900
Yeah, because you could jump back in the ring fast.

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:24.340
Yeah. You'd be, like, a jump in the air, like a somersault, and you're just back in the ring.

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:28.000
But the computer is, like, insistent, even though it knows that a count-out is gonna...

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:28.860
It's like, he'll come back out.

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:32.760
Yeah, like, the computer's, like, insistent on, like, as long as the player is out here,

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:33.900
I should be fighting him.

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:36.240
Never thinking, like, I should go back to the ring.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.060
There's a count-out coming up, you know?

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:42.220
Like, I think that's just weird, and to be honest, I said that the computer knows that,

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:43.840
but I highly doubt that it did.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:58.360
Right. So, we're bashing Data East here, but this game was actually developed by Technos Japan.

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:01.300
They did games...

00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:02.280
Technos? Technos.

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:07.660
I'm not pronouncing that right, but it's, like, it is techno, with an S at the end, but

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:10.040
the O has, like, a line over it.

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:11.560
Oh, okay. So...

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:14.100
I don't know what that is. It probably still makes it Technos, if you're asking me.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:15.840
Technos. Yeah.

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:17.220
They're also bankrupt.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:19.440
Oh, good. But they made...

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:23.100
They made a couple of notable games, so I don't know why they had such a hard time developing

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:24.720
this one, but they made Double Dragon.

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:27.400
They made River City Ransom.

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:29.220
Super Dodgeball.

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:30.520
Those are pretty good games.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:31.760
Yeah. All things considered.

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:33.700
Like, games that are still heard about.

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:35.440
Yeah. I don't know if they're, like, still good.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:37.380
I haven't gotten back to them in a long time, but...

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:38.880
Super Dodgeball's a fun game.

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:41.860
Yeah, Double Dragon is definitely gonna be, like, a highlight on NES.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:43.820
That'll be in there. I haven't played any of these games.

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:48.580
Very cool. That'll be a first for you, and you'll think, this is coming from the studio.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:50.380
It's made to Team Wrestling.

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:53.840
That's a big game? Double Dragon's a pretty big game, and I think it got a couple sequels, too.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:54.780
Yeah, with Battletoads.

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:56.080
Yeah, Double Dragon and Battletoads.

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:57.180
That's a big deal.

00:12:57.900 --> 00:12:58.940
Wait, they did Battletoads?

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:01.580
No, no, no. Well, okay, so there was a team-up.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:06.220
The franchise, yeah. Yeah. So Battletoads got its game, and then Double Dragon got its game, and then they actually,

